{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EhZR66LZ7UpHpeuJGmdzUn","type":"tool_result","content":"3:DB and Redis are required by the API.  Evolution and background workers are\n46:    max_workers=_PROBE_CONCURRENCY_LIMIT,\n54:    status: str\n56:    optional: dict[str, str]\n57:    workers: dict[str, str]\n60:    def http_status(self) -> int:\n61:        return 503 if self.status == \"not_ready\" else 200\n68:    def optional_failures(self) -> int:\n70:            state not in _OPTIONAL_HEALTHY_STATES for state in self.optional.values()\n71:        ) + sum(state != \"ok\" for state in self.workers.values())\n73:    def public_payload(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n75:            \"status\": self.status,\n78:            \"optional\": self.optional,\n79:            \"workers\": self.workers,\n106:                   WHERE status IN ('creating', 'reconciling')\n112:                   WHERE status IN ('creating', 'reconciling')\n130:def _check_redis_and_workers(settings: Settings) -> dict[str, str | None]:\n161:    # Authentication failures still prove that the optional service is reachable.\n162:    if response.status_code >= 500:\n237:    \"\"\"Collect required and optional states with one bounded timeout each.\"\"\"\n253:        lambda: _check_redis_and_workers(settings),\n282:    workers = _public_worker_states(\n288:    optional = {\n299:        status = \"not_ready\"\n301:        state not in _OPTIONAL_HEALTHY_STATES for state in optional.values()\n302:    ) or any(state != \"ok\" for state in workers.values()):\n303:        status = \"degraded\"\n305:        status = \"ready\"\n306:    return ReadinessReport(status, required, optional, workers)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f5f5b47-c66e-4591-b756-d99024a874c5","uuid":"81834525-b676-4031-96f3-30e897676665","timestamp":"2026-10-30T15:06:23.954Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"3:DB and Redis are required by the API.  Evolution and background workers are\n46:  